# Floe — Screens, the HUD, and audio

This file fixes the six screens, how a player moves between them, the readouts
the HUD carries, and the game's audio. The keys behind each action are in
`specs/controls.md`, and the run those screens frame is in
`specs/progression.md`.

## The screens

`screen` names the screen the game is showing, and `menuIndex` is the highlighted
item of whatever menu it carries, counted from `0`. The highlighted item is drawn
distinctly from the others.

| `screen` | What it shows |
| --- | --- |
| `title` | `TITLE_TEXT` (`FLOE`), `TAGLINE_TEXT` (`DON'T LOOK BACK`), and a vertical menu of `TITLE_ITEMS` (`CROSS`, `HOW TO PLAY`) in that order. A dim slice of the strait may show behind it. |
| `howto` | How to play, covered below. |
| `playing` | The live strait, the critter, the bears, and the HUD. |
| `paused` | The strait, visible and frozen, behind a menu of `PAUSE_ITEMS` (`RESUME`, `RESTART`, `QUIT TO MENU`) in that order. |
| `victory` | The final score, the levels cleared (`8`), the lives remaining, and a menu of `ENDING_ITEMS` (`PLAY AGAIN`, `MENU`) in that order. |
| `gameover` | The final score, the level reached (`reachedLevel`), and a menu of `ENDING_ITEMS` in that order. |

A freshly loaded build opens on `title` with `menuIndex` at `0`.

The `howto` screen names each of these: the goal of filling the five far-shore
bays, the keys the critter hops with, the bear that hunts the critter across the
whole strait, the vehicles sliding along the ice band, the floes drifting along
the water band, and the crossing timer.

## Moving between them

| Screen | Action | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `title` | Up, down | Moves `menuIndex` over `TITLE_ITEMS`, wrapping both ways. |
| `title` | Confirm | `CROSS` starts a run and opens `playing`; `HOW TO PLAY` opens `howto` with `menuIndex` at `0`. |
| `title` | Back | Nothing; the title screen is the outermost screen. |
| `howto` | Confirm, back | Returns to `title` with `HOW TO PLAY` selected, `TITLE_ITEMS` index `1`. |
| `playing` | Pause | Opens `paused` with `menuIndex` at `0`. |
| `paused` | Up, down | Moves `menuIndex` over `PAUSE_ITEMS`, wrapping both ways. |
| `paused` | Back | Returns to `playing`, resuming the crossing as it stood. |
| `paused` | Pause | Returns to `playing`, resuming the crossing as it stood. |
| `paused` | Confirm | `RESUME` returns to `playing`; `RESTART` starts a fresh run and opens `playing`; `QUIT TO MENU` returns to `title`. |
| `victory`, `gameover` | Up, down | Moves `menuIndex` over `ENDING_ITEMS`, wrapping both ways. |
| `victory`, `gameover` | Confirm | `PLAY AGAIN` starts a fresh run and opens `playing`; `MENU` returns to `title`. |
| `victory`, `gameover` | Back | Returns to `title`. |
| Every screen | Mute | Toggles the runtime's mute bit. |

Starting a run is what `specs/progression.md` fixes: level `1`, three lives, a
score of `0`, five open bays, and a fresh crossing. Resuming from `paused`
returns the crossing exactly as pausing left it, with the score, lives, level,
timer, bays, critter, and bears untouched.

Every route back to `title` selects the entry it left by. `QUIT TO MENU`, `MENU`,
and Back from `victory` or `gameover` all return to `title` with `CROSS`
selected, `TITLE_ITEMS` index `0`, `CROSS` being the entry that started the run.

Where several of a menu's edges arrive on one tick, up is applied before down and
movement before confirm, so a tick carrying both an up edge and a down edge moves
up only, and a tick carrying a movement edge and a confirm edge moves only.

### Pointer and touch

Each menu item occupies a rectangular hit region the build lays out. Every region
lies inside the `1280 x 720` stage, and no two items of one menu share a point, so
a pointer is over at most one entry. `specs/instrumentation.md` states the reading
through which the build reports an item's region in logical units, so the menus
keep the layout the build chose.

| Input | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| A pointer moves onto an item's region | `menuIndex` becomes that item's index. |
| A touch contact lands inside an item's region, or travels onto one | `menuIndex` becomes that item's index. |
| A pointer is pressed and released inside one item's region | `menuIndex` becomes that item's index, and that item is confirmed. |
| A touch contact lands and lifts inside one item's region | `menuIndex` becomes that item's index, and that item is confirmed. |

A confirm requires both of its edges inside one item's region: the press and its
release for a pointer, the landing and the lift for a touch contact. Two edges
that fall in different regions, and an edge that falls outside every region,
confirm no item. A press and the release that follows it may arrive on one tick,
and that tick confirms.

All four menus are driven this way: `TITLE_ITEMS` on `title`, `PAUSE_ITEMS` on
`paused`, and `ENDING_ITEMS` on `victory` and on `gameover`. The item every
confirm acts on is the item at `menuIndex`, whichever input raised it, and the
effect is the one the transition table gives Confirm on that screen.

## The HUD

The HUD bar is the full-width strip above the strait that `specs/strait.md`
fixes, and it carries five readouts. Their arrangement and styling are yours;
each is inside the bar and legible against it.

| Readout | Shows |
| --- | --- |
| Score | The running score. |
| Lives | `lives`, the lives the run has left counting the critter currently crossing, so a run that has lost none reads `3`. |
| Level | `HUD_LEVEL_LABEL` (`LEVEL`), the current `level`, and `TOTAL_LEVELS` (`8`). |
| Timer | The seconds left on the crossing timer, following `timer`. |
| Bays | One mark per bay, in the bays' own left-to-right order, each showing whether that bay is filled. |

Nothing drawn on the strait is drawn inside the HUD bar.

## Audio

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
This game stands on no engine, so the audio is yours to write. Synthesize the
cues with the Web Audio API rather than shipping audio files, hold a mute bit
that the mute action toggles, and start no sound until the player has interacted
with the page.
{{else}}
Audio plays through the {{engine.name}} engine's cue bus, which it documents in
the `engine/` directory at the root of this repository. Define each cue under the
name `CUES` gives it and play it through the bus. Muting and the first-interaction
unlock are the engine's: the mute action toggles the engine's own mute bit.
{{/if}}

Ten cues, one per event, each a distinct short sound so the events are told apart
by ear.

| Cue | Played when |
| --- | --- |
| `hop` | An accepted hop is taken. A refused hop plays nothing. |
| `splash` | The critter falls into open water or is carried off a side edge. |
| `crush` | A vehicle crushes the critter. |
| `caught` | A bear catches the critter. |
| `bay` | A crossing ends in a bay. |
| `level-clear` | A level below `TOTAL_LEVELS` is cleared. |
| `bonus-life` | The score earns a bonus life. |
| `victory` | The run is won. |
| `game-over` | The death that empties the lives. |
| `menu` | A menu's highlight moves, once per move. |

Each is played on the tick its event happens, once per tick however many times
the event was raised within it. The game stays fully playable with sound muted,
and it never fails to run or load when audio cannot start.

## Out of scope

- Network play, and any progress saved between sessions.
- Gamepad input.
- Power-ups, weapons, alternate straits, and difficulty menus. The game is the
  one strait and the one eight-level run.
